SonarQube



SonarQube is a code quality and security analysis tool used in the **CI/CD pipeline**.

### What it checks

* 🐛 **Bugs** – coding errors
* 🔐 **Vulnerabilities** – security issues
* 🧹 **Code Smells** – maintainability problems
* 📊 **Code Coverage** – how much code is tested
* 🔁 **Duplications** – duplicate code

```







\### Important terms



| Term             | Meaning                                       |

| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------- |

| \*\*SonarQube\*\*    | Server/UI that stores and analyzes results    |

| \*\*SonarScanner\*\* | Tool that scans source code                   |

| \*\*Project Key\*\*  | Unique ID of the project                      |

| \*\*Token\*\*        | Authentication credential                     |

| \*\*Quality Gate\*\* | Pass/fail criteria for code quality           |

| \*\*Dashboard\*\*    | Shows bugs, vulnerabilities, smells, coverage |



\*\*Interview one-liner:\*\*



> “SonarQube is used in CI/CD to perform static code analysis and identify bugs, vulnerabilities, code smells, coverage, and duplication before deployment.”

















